{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"{\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"ffd4f239-62a6-4457-8f66-1e2bc3b1e6a9\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 12, which defines “the State” for Fundamental Rights, appears in which Part of the Constitution?\",\"hi\":\"मौलिक अधिकारों के लिए “राज्य” को परिभाषित करने वाला अनुच्छेद 12 संविधान के किस भाग में है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Part III\",\"hi\":\"भाग III\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Part II\",\"hi\":\"भाग II\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Part IV\",\"hi\":\"भाग IV\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Part V\",\"hi\":\"भाग V\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=37 — Part III, Article 12, PDF page 37 (document page 7)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=37\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 12, PDF page 37 (document page 7)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Article 12, official PDF page 37 (document page 7)\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fbe23b99-e762-4f14-b3cf-317c6b6f14a5\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What does Article 13(4) say about a constitutional amendment made under Article 368?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 13(4), अनुच्छेद 368 के अधीन किए गए संविधान संशोधन के बारे में क्या कहता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"It is automatically void\",\"hi\":\"वह स्वतः शून्य है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"It requires approval by every court\",\"hi\":\"उसे प्रत्येक न्यायालय की स्वीकृति चाहिए\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Article 13 does not apply to it\",\"hi\":\"उस पर अनुच्छेद 13 लागू नहीं होता\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"It becomes an ordinary rule\",\"hi\":\"वह साधारण नियम बन जाता है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=37 — Part III, Article 13 and Twenty-fourth Amendment footnote, PDF page 37 (document page 6); Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=260 — Part XX, Article 368(3), PDF page 260 (document page 229); Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/28469.pdf#page=5 — Judgment, PDF pages 5-7: Shankari Prasad, Sajjan Singh, Golaknath, Twenty-fourth Amendment and Kesavananda Bharati\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=37\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 13 and Twenty-fourth Amendment footnote, PDF page 37 (document page 6)\"},{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=260\",\"citation\":\"Part XX, Article 368(3), PDF page 260 (document page 229)\"},{\"title\":\"I.R. Coelho v. State of Tamil Nadu, (2007) 2 SCC 1\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/28469.pdf#page=5\",\"citation\":\"Judgment, PDF pages 5-7: Shankari Prasad, Sajjan Singh, Golaknath, Twenty-fourth Amendment and Kesavananda Bharati\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Articles 13(4) and 368(3), official PDF pages 37 and 260; I.R. Coelho v. State of Tamil Nadu, official Supreme Court PDF pages 5-7\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f86e061a-6d86-4c9f-b761-4369562e7232\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which two conditions form the classic Article 14 test of permissible classification?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 14 के अधीन अनुमेय वर्गीकरण की पारंपरिक कसौटी किन दो शर्तों से बनती है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Intelligible differentia and a rational relation to the statutory object\",\"hi\":\"बोधगम्य विभेद और विधि के उद्देश्य से युक्तियुक्त संबंध\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Unanimous approval and retrospective operation\",\"hi\":\"सर्वसम्मत स्वीकृति और भूतलक्षी प्रवर्तन\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Presidential order and judicial appointment\",\"hi\":\"राष्ट्रपति आदेश और न्यायिक नियुक्ति\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Religious identity and residence only\",\"hi\":\"केवल धार्मिक पहचान और निवास\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/864.pdf#page=3 — Judgment, PDF page 3: Article 14 permits reasonable classification subject to intelligible differentia and rational nexus\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Budhan Choudhry v. State of Bihar, 1955 1 SCR 1045\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/864.pdf#page=3\",\"citation\":\"Judgment, PDF page 3: Article 14 permits reasonable classification subject to intelligible differentia and rational nexus\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Budhan Choudhry v. State of Bihar, official Supreme Court PDF page 3\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f86b6445-c826-4ca2-98c7-bf42f64164df\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which sequence best states the I.R. Coelho test for a post-24 April 1973 Ninth Schedule law?\",\"hi\":\"24 अप्रैल 1973 के बाद नौवीं अनुसूची में रखी विधि के लिए आई.आर. कोएल्हो की कसौटी का सही क्रम क्या है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Check only whether Parliament used the word “amendment”\",\"hi\":\"केवल जाँचें कि संसद ने “संशोधन” शब्द प्रयोग किया\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Assume automatic immunity and end review\",\"hi\":\"स्वतः उन्मुक्ति मानकर जाँच समाप्त करें\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Review only the law’s title\",\"hi\":\"केवल विधि का शीर्षक जाँचें\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"First identify Part III infringement, then assess its impact on basic structure; invalidate if the impact destroys or damages basic structure\",\"hi\":\"पहले भाग III के उल्लंघन को पहचानें, फिर मूल संरचना पर उसके प्रभाव की जाँच करें; प्रभाव मूल संरचना को नष्ट या क्षतिग्रस्त करे तो अमान्य ठहराएँ\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/28469.pdf#page=40 — Conclusion, PDF pages 40-41: post-24 April 1973 Ninth Schedule amendments, rights/impact test and basic-structure review\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"I.R. Coelho v. State of Tamil Nadu, (2007) 2 SCC 1\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/28469.pdf#page=40\",\"citation\":\"Conclusion, PDF pages 40-41: post-24 April 1973 Ninth Schedule amendments, rights/impact test and basic-structure review\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"I.R. Coelho v. State of Tamil Nadu, conclusion, official Supreme Court PDF pages 40-41\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f4187a8b-cf06-47d9-9120-e28668298b56\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 15(2)(b) covers the use of which facilities when maintained from State funds or dedicated to public use?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 15(2)(b) राज्य निधि से पोषित या सार्वजनिक उपयोग के लिए समर्पित किन सुविधाओं के उपयोग को आच्छादित करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Only private bedrooms\",\"hi\":\"केवल निजी शयनकक्ष\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Only legislative chambers\",\"hi\":\"केवल विधायी सदन\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Only foreign embassies\",\"hi\":\"केवल विदेशी दूतावास\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Wells, tanks, bathing ghats, roads and places of public resort\",\"hi\":\"कुएँ, तालाब, स्नानघाट, सड़कें और सार्वजनिक समागम-स्थान\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=38 — Part III, Article 15(2)-(6) and amendment footnotes, PDF page 38 (document page 7); National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT) — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps202.pdf#page=6 — Printed pages 31-33, PDF pages 6-8: Right to Equality, equal access, reservation, untouchability and titles\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=38\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 15(2)-(6) and amendment footnotes, PDF page 38 (document page 7)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 2: Rights in the Indian Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps202.pdf#page=6\",\"citation\":\"Printed pages 31-33, PDF pages 6-8: Right to Equality, equal access, reservation, untouchability and titles\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Article 15(2)-(6), official PDF page 38; NCERT Class XI, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 2, printed pages 31-33\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f2fae112-94d5-453d-acd8-aa5e0c5764cf\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which condition is essential before a custom or usage is treated as “law” under Article 13(3)(a)?\",\"hi\":\"किस शर्त के पूरा होने पर रूढ़ि या प्रथा को अनुच्छेद 13(3)(a) के अधीन “विधि” माना जाता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"It must be written in English\",\"hi\":\"उसे अंग्रेज़ी में लिखा होना चाहिए\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"It must be older than one hundred years\",\"hi\":\"वह सौ वर्ष से पुरानी होनी चाहिए\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"It must be approved by every State Legislature\",\"hi\":\"उसे हर राज्य विधानमंडल की स्वीकृति होनी चाहिए\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"It must have the force of law in the territory of India\",\"hi\":\"भारत के राज्यक्षेत्र में उसे विधि का बल प्राप्त होना चाहिए\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=37 — Part III, Article 13 and Twenty-fourth Amendment footnote, PDF page 37 (document page 6)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=37\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 13 and Twenty-fourth Amendment footnote, PDF page 37 (document page 6)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Article 13, official PDF page 37\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f237a17a-c7bc-44e0-9a37-4e767f978c3d\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What does Article 16(5) protect from being invalidated by Article 16?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 16(5) किस व्यवस्था को अनुच्छेद 16 के कारण अमान्य होने से बचाता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Hereditary political titles\",\"hi\":\"वंशानुगत राजनीतिक उपाधियाँ\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Discrimination in every private job\",\"hi\":\"हर निजी नौकरी में भेदभाव\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"All residence requirements made by executives\",\"hi\":\"कार्यपालिका द्वारा बनाई सभी निवास अपेक्षाएँ\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"A law requiring an office connected with a religious or denominational institution to be held by a person professing that religion or denomination\",\"hi\":\"धार्मिक या सांप्रदायिक संस्था से जुड़े पद को उस धर्म या संप्रदाय को मानने वाले व्यक्ति द्वारा धारण करने की अपेक्षा वाली विधि\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=40 — Part III, Articles 16(5)-(6), 17 and 18, PDF page 40 (document page 9)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=40\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Articles 16(5)-(6), 17 and 18, PDF page 40 (document page 9)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Articles 16(5)-(6), 17 and 18, official PDF page 40\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f16bfee9-3ceb-45bc-9758-e2f57960d992\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"In Ajay Hasia, why was the Regional Engineering College society held to be an “authority” under Article 12?\",\"hi\":\"अजय हसिया में क्षेत्रीय इंजीनियरिंग महाविद्यालय की सोसाइटी को अनुच्छेद 12 के अधीन “प्राधिकारी” क्यों माना गया?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The established facts showed deep governmental financing, control, direction and dominance over its governing structure\",\"hi\":\"स्थापित तथ्यों से उसके शासी ढाँचे पर गहन सरकारी वित्तपोषण, नियंत्रण, निर्देशन और प्रभुत्व सिद्ध हुआ\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Every educational institution is automatically State\",\"hi\":\"प्रत्येक शैक्षणिक संस्था स्वतः राज्य है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"It was located in a capital city\",\"hi\":\"वह राजधानी में स्थित थी\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Its students received degrees\",\"hi\":\"उसके विद्यार्थियों को उपाधियाँ मिलती थीं\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/4414.pdf#page=19 — Judgment, PDF page 19: application of the test to the Regional Engineering College society\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Ajay Hasia v. Khalid Mujib Sehravardi, (1981) 1 SCC 722\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/4414.pdf#page=19\",\"citation\":\"Judgment, PDF page 19: application of the test to the Regional Engineering College society\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Ajay Hasia v. Khalid Mujib Sehravardi, official Supreme Court PDF page 19\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f1155b81-89fd-448e-9a3d-69876345b566\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"How does the Protection of Civil Rights Act, 1955 define “civil rights”?\",\"hi\":\"सिविल अधिकार संरक्षण अधिनियम, 1955 “सिविल अधिकार” को कैसे परिभाषित करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Any contractual right\",\"hi\":\"कोई भी संविदात्मक अधिकार\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Only voting rights\",\"hi\":\"केवल मतदान अधिकार\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A right accruing to a person by reason of the abolition of untouchability by Article 17\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 17 द्वारा अस्पृश्यता के अंत के कारण किसी व्यक्ति को प्राप्त अधिकार\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Only property rights\",\"hi\":\"केवल संपत्ति अधिकार\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: India Code, Legislative Department, Government of India — https://www.indiacode.nic.in/bitstream/123456789/15434/1/protection_of_civil_rights_act%2C_1955.pdf#page=2 — Long title and Sections 1-2, PDF page 2: punishment for untouchability disabilities and definition of civil rights by reference to Article 17; Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=40 — Part III, Articles 16(5)-(6), 17 and 18, PDF page 40 (document page 9)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Protection of Civil Rights Act, 1955 (Act 22 of 1955)\",\"institution\":\"India Code, Legislative Department, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.indiacode.nic.in/bitstream/123456789/15434/1/protection_of_civil_rights_act%2C_1955.pdf#page=2\",\"citation\":\"Long title and Sections 1-2, PDF page 2: punishment for untouchability disabilities and definition of civil rights by reference to Article 17\"},{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=40\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Articles 16(5)-(6), 17 and 18, PDF page 40 (document page 9)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Protection of Civil Rights Act, 1955, Sections 1-2, o